 </tr>\r\n</tbody></table>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;line-height:115%\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"> </span></p>\r\n\r\n<pre style=\"line-height:11.25pt;background:white;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\" lang=\"EN-US\">Here, I got the warning that some estimated ov variances were negative, although all error variances were constrained to be positive. </span></pre><pre style=\"line-height:11.25pt;background:white;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\" lang=\"EN-US\"> </span></pre><pre style=\"line-height:11.25pt;background:white;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\" lang=\"EN-US\">How is this possible? What was false in the model syntax of m2?</span></pre><pre style=\"line-height:11.25pt;background:white;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\" lang=\"EN-US\"> </span></pre><pre style=\"line-height:11.25pt;background:white;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\" lang=\"EN-US\">Thanks in advance for all your responses!</span></pre><pre style=\"line-height:11.25pt;background:white;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\" lang=\"EN-US\"> </span></pre><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\" lang=\"EN-US\">Best,<br>\r\nAlodie </span></div>"
